<h2>Topic 2: Multiple Lives - Joint Life and Last Survivor</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain joint life and last survivor, calculate probabilities, explain uses.</p>
<p>Many policies cover two lives - husband and wife, business partners.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Joint life status (xy):</b> Alive while BOTH are alive. Ends when first dies. Survival: tpxy = tpx x tpy, if independent.</p><p><b>Last survivor status (xy-bar):</b> Alive while AT LEAST ONE is alive. Ends when second dies. Survival: tpxy-bar = tpx + tpy - tpxy.</p><p><b>Example:</b> px = 0.99, py = 0.98. Joint survival = 0.99 x 0.98 = 0.9702. Last survivor survival = 0.99 + 0.98 - 0.9702 = 0.9998.</p></div><p><b>Uses:</b> Joint life assurance pays on first death - for mortgage. Last survivor annuity pays until second dies - for couple's pension.</p>
