<h2>Topic 3: Multiple Decrements</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain multiple decrements, distinguish death vs withdrawal, calculate probabilities.</p>
<p>A person can leave a pension scheme by death, withdrawal, retirement, or ill-health. That is multiple decrements - many ways out.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Single decrement:</b> Only death. <b>Multiple decrement:</b> Death + Withdrawal + Retirement.</p><p><b>Example:</b> 1000 members. In a year, 10 die, 50 withdraw, 20 retire. Total leaving = 80. Probability of leaving by death = 10/1000 = 0.01. By withdrawal = 0.05. By retirement = 0.02. Total decrement = 0.08.</p><p><b>Key:</b> Decrements compete. If many withdraw, fewer remain to die later.</p></div>
