<h2>Topic 4: Pensions and Retirement Benefits</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain pension, explain defined benefit vs defined contribution, calculate pension.</p>
<p>Pension pays income in retirement. It is the biggest long-term promise an actuary prices.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Defined Benefit (DB):</b> Pension is promised by formula, e.g. 1/60 x Final Salary x Years. Employer bears risk.</p><p><b>Defined Contribution (DC):</b> Contributions are fixed, pension depends on investment. Member bears risk.</p><p><b>Example DB:</b> Final salary 1200000, years 30, accrual 1/60. Pension = 1200000 x 30 / 60 = 600000 per year.</p></div>
