<h2>Topic 5: Profit Testing</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain profit testing, project cashflows, explain profit signature and NPV.</p>
<p>Profit testing asks: If we sell this policy, how much profit will we make each year? It projects cashflows year by year.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Year cashflow:</b> Premium + Interest - Expenses - Claims - Change in Reserve = Profit that year.</p><p><b>Profit signature:</b> Profit in year 1, year 2, year 3, ...</p><p><b>NPV of profit:</b> Discount profit signature at risk discount rate. If NPV > 0, product is profitable.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Year 1 profit -1000 (new business strain), Year 2 profit 500, Year 3 profit 600. NPV at 10% = -1000 + 500/1.1 + 600/1.21 = -1000 + 455 + 496 = -49. Not profitable at 10%.</p></div>
