<h2>Topic 6: Reserves and Valuation</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain reserve, calculate prospective reserve, explain valuation and solvency.</p>
<p>Reserve is money held today to pay future claims. Valuation checks if reserves are enough.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Prospective reserve:</b> tV = PV Future Benefits - PV Future Premiums.</p><p><b>Example:</b> At time 5, PV Future Benefits = 80000, PV Future Premiums = 30000. Reserve = 50000.</p><p><b>Valuation:</b> Actuary checks reserves using prudent assumptions. If reserves are too low, company is insolvent - it cannot pay. Regulator (IRA) requires valuation every year.</p></div>
